    "music": null,
    "description": {
      "text": "\tEarth is also the capital of the Republic. Representative government becomes complicated when one planet has a greater population than a hundred planets elsewhere. As a result, smaller settlements are grouped together into planetary districts that elect a single representative between them - a source of much frustration in the frontier worlds.",
      "toDisplay": null
    },
    "spaceport": {
      "text": "\tInside the towers is a warren of dim hallways and dingy shops. Hitchhikers sleep in the corners of unused docking bays under old army blankets, a few uniformed cleaners try to keep the litter and dust in check, and rich tourists from other stars cling tightly to their expensive cameras.",
      "toDisplay": null
    },
